{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Frames the app hands in from outside a capture session, such as a decoded network stream, for a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"CapturePreviewView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to draw as it draws a capture card.","type":"text"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Showing-the-stream","generated":true,"title":"Showing the stream","identifiers":["doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CapturePreviewSource"]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/FrameFeed"},"metadata":{"role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"HeadwireCapture"}],"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"FrameFeed","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"FrameFeed","roleHeading":"Class","symbolKind":"class","externalID":"s:15HeadwireCapture9FrameFeedC","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"FrameFeed","kind":"identifier"}]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"final","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"FrameFeed","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["iOS","iPadOS","Mac Catalyst"]}]},{"mentions":["doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CapturePipeline"],"kind":"mentions"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Its frames take the Metal path whatever the upscaling setting, so fit, fill, zoom, the reported"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"layout, and MetalFX all apply; with upscaling off they are drawn in one bilinear pass. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"displayed size is the newest frame’s, and the content is always the whole frame, since a stream"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"has no padding. Each sample must carry a "},{"code":"CVPixelBuffer","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in a layout the front end reads, such"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as "},{"code":"420f","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"420v","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Frames are drawn on the feed’s own queue, newest first: a frame that arrives while another is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"still waiting replaces it. The newest frame is kept, so the picture stays on screen until the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"next one, and is drawn again after a relayout or when a new view attaches."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Initializers","generated":true,"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/FrameFeed\/init()"]},{"anchor":"Instance-Properties","generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/FrameFeed\/mirror","doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/FrameFeed\/tap"]},{"anchor":"Instance-Methods","generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/FrameFeed\/frameSizes()","doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/FrameFeed\/send(_:)"]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/headwirecapture\/framefeed"]}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireC